  "description": "Change of use from Use Class C3 (dwelling house) to Use Class C4 (HMO-house in multiple occupation) with associated cycle and refuse storage involving single storey rear extension, rear dormer and outrigger dormer with front rooflights.",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development to which this permission relates must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of the decision notice. \r\rReason: To comply with the provisions of S.51 of the Planning & Compulsory Purchase Act 2004.\r",
    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans:\rE00\rP00\rP01\rP02\rP03\rP04\rP05\rP06\rP07\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning.\r",
    "Prior to first occupation of the HMO, Cycle parking, shall be provided as indicated on drawing P01, in accordance with the following requirements and maintained as such thereafter:\r\r- Provision of a minimum of SIX long stay cycle parking spaces;\r\r- in an accessible location; the store door must have a minimum opening width of 1.2m\r\r- long stay cycle parking spaces secured with a British Standard mortice lock or access fob;\r\r- fully enclosed: 4 walls and a roof.\r\rReason: To ensure the provision of accessible, secure, and adequate cycle parking facilities and to safeguard the character and appearance of the area.\r\r",
    "Notwithstanding the details shown on the submitted drawings, prior to the first occupation of the HMO hereby permitted, waste storage and recycling facilities to satisfy the permitted number of occupiers shall have been provided on site, in accordance with the Enfield's Household Recycling and Waste Planning Guidance for New Developments (February 2024). Such facilities are to be retained thereafter, unless otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority.\r\rReason: In the interests of amenity and the recycling of waste materials in support of the Boroughs waste reduction targets.\r",
    "The use of the property as a House in Multiple Occupation hereby approved shall be occupied by a maximum of 6 people at any one time and shall not be subdivided or occupied as self-contained units. \r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.\r",
    "No independent cooking or laundry facilities shall be installed in any of the respective bedrooms and the ground floor communal kitchen living and dining room, shall be retained in perpetuity. \r\rReason: To accord with the stipulations of definition as a House of Multiple Occupation and to safeguard the residential character of the surrounding area.\r"
  ],
